  "verbalization": "Isoliquiritigenin is implicated in the inhibition of RAF proto-oncogene serine/threonine-protein kinase through a multi-step mechanism involving the target Interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha. The evidence suggests that Isoliquiritigenin acts as a target of multiple compounds, including 2-Phenylpropan-1-Ol and (1S,13Z,17R,18R)-9-Hydroxy-4,5-dimethoxy-16-oxa-23-azapentacyclo[15.7.1.18,12.02,7.018,23]hexacosa-2,4,6,8,10,12(26),13-heptaen-15-one, which in turn target RAF proto-oncogene serine/threonine-protein kinase. This indicates that Isoliquiritigenin may exert its biological effects through a shared pathway, possibly by modulating the signaling cascade initiated by the Interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway suggests that Isoliquiritigenin may act as a modulator of the RAF kinase pathway, potentially through a mechanism involving the inhibition of downstream signaling events. The evidence supports a plausible mechanistic link between Isoliquiritigenin and RAF proto-oncogene serine/threonine-protein kinase, though further experimental validation is required to confirm the direct interaction and the specific molecular mechanism involved.",
